This product includes data and assets from third-party sources:

* The Linear A inscription corpus (public/corpus/) is derived from the
  mwenge/lineara.xyz repository (https://github.com/mwenge/lineara.xyz),
  which transcribes the GORILA volumes by Louis Godart and Jean-Pierre
  Olivier (École Française d'Athènes, 1976-1985).

* Pre-2024 commentary HTML mirrored in public/upstream/commentary/ derives
  from John G. Younger's Linear A material, formerly hosted at
  people.ku.edu/~jyounger/LinearA/ (retired 2024). Younger's current
  material is published as PDFs at
  https://www.academia.edu/117949722/Younger_JG_Linear_A_folder_introduction.

* Facsimile drawings and photographs of Linear A inscriptions
  (public/upstream/images/) are © École Française d'Athènes and are
  redistributed here for academic reference only under fair-use principles.
  Image rights remain with the École Française d'Athènes and are NOT
  granted under the Apache 2.0 license that covers the rest of this work.

* GORILA PDF citations (public/upstream/papers/) are © École Française
  d'Athènes and are bundled for academic reference only on the same terms.

* The UI webfonts are self-hosted in public/fonts/ and are all licensed
  under the SIL Open Font License 1.1: Noto Sans Linear A (Google — renders
  the Linear A glyphs), Inter (Rasmus Andersson), JetBrains Mono (JetBrains),
  and Crimson Pro (Jacques Le Bailly).
